# R8 rules of the application, merged by AGP with
# proguard-android-optimize.txt (applied by default) and with the rules every
# library ships in its artefact.
#
# Every keep rule is code R8 gives up removing, so none is written without a
# reason. The libraries that rely on reflection already carry their own
# (checked with -printconfiguration on AGP 9.3.3):
#
# - kotlinx.serialization 1.11 keeps the generated serialisers and their
#   companions; the parser calls them directly anyway (plugin, no reflection).
# - Room 2.8 keeps the no-argument constructor of every RoomDatabase subclass,
#   which is how it instantiates PotableDatabase_Impl.
# - WorkManager 2.11 keeps the name and the (Context, WorkerParameters)
#   constructor of every ListenableWorker: AlertWorker is rebuilt by its class
#   name, which stays stable from one release to the next.
# - DataStore ships the rules of its embedded protobuf; OkHttp and the
#   coroutines theirs.
#
# The view models are built by explicit factories and the navigation routes
# are strings: nothing else is reached by reflection.

# Readable stack traces in a bug report (the mapping file stays private).
# Measured: the APK keeps the same size to the byte.
-keepattributes SourceFile, LineNumberTable
-renamesourcefileattribute SourceFile
